# Fleet votes and their callbacks. House style: content/STYLE.md.

card m_carrier
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 13 16
roles A
when cond A ok
text The high-gain antenna on {A}'s ship logs a weak carrier on a channel the fleet stopped using years ago, coming and going every 11 seconds. {A} files it for the morning report under "retired hardware, probably", and then, because the form has a box for it, under "courtesy".
do open dec_signal

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
days 13 16
weight 5
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
text The old-channel carrier is still there this morning, patient as a dripping tap. {A} wants to turn a dish and answer it, if only to be polite. {B} points out that turning the dish costs propellant the fleet hasn't got to spare, for a conversation with a machine.
option open | Answer it | {A} spends the propellant, and the fleet sends one plain hail on the old channel. Then an hour of static. The carrier comes and goes exactly as before. {A} logs the time the hail went out, to the second, out of habit.
  set signal_answered
  mark t_signal
  res fuel -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | Log it, keep going | The carrier goes into the anomaly log under "later". {A} tapes a printout of the waveform above the bunk, just in case.
  set signal_ignored
  mark t_signal
  morale A -5

card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 39
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when since t_signal >= 14
text At 03:12 the dish catches a reply on the old channel: half a frame of housekeeping telemetry in a format nobody has flown in years, cut off mid-header, as if the sender restarted mid-sentence. {A} is the only one awake. Mission Control answers 40 minutes later: "say again??"
do set signal_contact
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 39
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when since t_signal >= 14
text {A} finds the carrier in the dish logs again. It's stronger now, and its bearing has crept toward the arrival corridor, a little more each day. Nobody uses the word "following". The anomaly report uses the word "persistent", and leaves it there.
do set echo_heard
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
text A micrometeoroid hits the hull during {A}'s EVA, close enough to feel through the boots. {A} secures every tool, works back along the tether hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when bestbond B A
text {A} needs a medical kit from another ship, and the next transfer window is tight.
option send | Send the kit | A kit crosses on the next transfer. {A}'s wrist is splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} doesn't wait for the paperwork, makes the crossing in the next window, and splints the wrist personally. The mission log calls it "nominal". Six ships read the log, and every one of them knows better.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4
